    },
    "text": "Lake Formation cross-account sharing issues usually come down to a handful of specific checks \u2014 RAM share acceptance, resource link creation in the consumer account, actual LF permission grants, and the consumer's data lake settings. I can check these for you, but I need a few specifics first:\n\n1. **Producer (sharing) account ID** and **Glue database name**\n2. **Consumer account ID** that should be seeing it\n3. **Region**\n4. Was this shared via **named resource** grants or **LF-Tags**?\n\nOnce I have those, I'll check the Lake Formation permissions on the database, the RAM resource share status, and whether the consumer side has accepted/created the resource link."
